It's difficult to discern from your post how challenging a feral
Arch-lich would be, but it might very well have leveled up
significantly over its time working for you.  As such, it's quite
possible for it to appear hostile or at least annoying at an
inconvenient time.  Therefore, I would search up and down levels with
your towel and whistle until you find it and then strand it in the top
of Sokoban or the bottom of the mines.  One thing to note, former pets
with teleport are still able to teleport to you once they have gone
wild, even when peaceful.  It's very annoying to be crossing a level
with an arch-lich that keeps teleporting right in front of you without
the opportunity to displace it; even worse is when they teleport to you
and start attacking.

I have been working with pets quite a bit lately and the next time that
I get a high level lich the first thing on my "to-do" list will be to
find a cockatrice corpse.

Hopefully someone else can comment on the best search pattern for you.


